.TH SSHC 1 "2026-10-05" "sshc 0.5.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
sshc \- ssh, scp, sftp and rsync that answer the password prompt for you
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sshc
[\fBssh\fR] [\fIssh options\fR] \fIdestination\fR [\fIcommand\fR ...]
.br
.B sshc
\fBscp\fR | \fBsftp\fR | \fBrsync\fR | \fBssh\-copy\-id\fR | \fBssh\-add\fR [\fIoptions\fR] ...
.br
.B sshc set
[\fB\-s\fR] [\fB\-p\fR] [\fB\-H\fR \fIhost\fR] [\fB\-k\fR \fIkey\fR] [\fB\-P\fR \fIprofile\fR] [\fB\-c\fR \fIcommand\fR] [\fIvalue\fR]
.br
.B sshc
\fBunset\fR | \fBlist\fR | \fBcheck\fR | \fBuse\fR | \fBmigrate\fR | \fBhosts\fR | \fBpick\fR | \fBeach\fR | \fBrun\fR | \fBupdate\fR | \fBdoctor\fR ...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B sshc
runs the OpenSSH client that is already installed and answers its prompt for
a login password, or for the passphrase of an SSH key, from a secret you have
stored. It does this through OpenSSH's own
.B SSH_ASKPASS
hook, so every option of the wrapped tool keeps working and the secret is
never placed on a command line.
.PP
Everything after the optional tool name is handed to that tool unchanged.
A host key confirmation, a password change and any other prompt are passed
to the terminal as usual.
.SH STORING SECRETS
.TP
.B sshc set \-s
Keep the secret for this terminal only, in an environment variable. Needs the
shell hook (see
.BR "SHELL HOOK" ).
.TP
.B sshc set
Save it in the system's credential store: Windows Credential Manager, the
macOS Keychain or the Secret Service keyring on Linux. Where there is none,
or with
.BR \-\-plain ,
it is kept in the config file in plain text.
.TP
.BI "sshc set \-c " command
Store nothing. Run
.I command
\- a password manager's command-line tool \- whenever the secret is needed and
use the first line it prints.
.BR %h ,
.B %u
and
.B %k
stand for the host, user and key file. The command is run directly, not by a
shell.
.PP
Add
.B \-p
for a key passphrase instead of a login password,
.BI \-H " host"
for one host,
.BI \-k " key"
for one key,
.BI \-P " profile"
for a profile other than the active one, and
.B \-o
(with
.B \-H
and
.BR \-c )
for the one-time code a host asks for after the password.
.B sshc unset
takes the same options and removes an entry;
.B sshc list
shows what is stored and where, never the values.
.SH OTHER COMMANDS
.TP
.BI "sshc check " destination
Show which stored secret a connection would use, without connecting.
.TP
.BR "sshc use " [\fIname\fR]
Show or switch the active profile.
.TP
.B sshc migrate
Move plain-text entries into the credential store.
.TP
.BR sshc ", " "sshc pick"
Pick a host from the ssh config and connect to it.
.B sshc hosts
lists them.
.TP
.BI "sshc each " "host ... " \-\- " command"
Run a command on several hosts at once.
.TP
.BI "sshc run " command
Run any program that uses ssh underneath, such as git, with its prompts
answered. The active login password is only offered to hosts named with
.BR \-d .
.TP
.B sshc ssh\-add
Unlock a key into ssh\-agent with the stored passphrase.
.TP
.BR "sshc update " [ \-\-check ]
Install the latest release.
.TP
.B sshc doctor
Check the setup and say how to fix what is wrong.
.TP
.BR "sshc install" ", " "sshc init" ", " "sshc shell\-init"
Install for the current user, create a config file template, print the shell
hook.
.SH SHELL HOOK
.B sshc set \-s
and
.B sshc use
change the environment of the running shell, which only shell code can do,
and Tab completion is shell code as well. Load the hook from the shell's
startup file:
.PP
.nf
    eval "$(sshc shell\-init bash)"        # bash, zsh
    sshc shell\-init fish | source         # fish
.fi
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.BR SSHC_PASSWORD ", " SSHC_PASSPHRASE
The active login password and key passphrase.
.TP
.BR SSHC_PASSWORD_ \fIHOST\fR ", " SSHC_PASSPHRASE_ \fIKEYFILE\fR
The same for one host or key; the name is upper-cased, with every other
character replaced by an underscore.
.TP
.B SSHC_PROFILE
The active profile.
.TP
.B SSHC_CONFIG
The config file to use.
.TP
.B SSHC_CREDENTIAL_STORE
Set to
.B off
to keep away from the credential store.
.TP
.B SSHC_NO_PROMPT
If set, never ask on the terminal; fail instead. For scripts.
.TP
.B SSHC_DEBUG
If set, print what sshc decides at each step, never a secret.
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
If set, do not colour the output.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I sshc.conf
Next to the executable, or in
.I ~/.config/sshc/
when that directory is not writable or belongs to a package manager. It
records which entries exist and holds settings; it must be readable by its
owner only.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ssh (1),
.BR scp (1),
.BR sftp (1),
.BR ssh\-add (1),
.BR ssh\-agent (1)
.PP
Full documentation: https://github.com/W-Industries-Luke/sshc
